{"parentUuid":"7824fa93-e4de-4f9d-8bb7-996dfcebb097","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGP16YLo9jNXsoUcVgDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RodpuhR66ZYUeTyg3Jys1V","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22 (three commits, each checked against real reference frames viewed this turn):\n  References viewed in the browser pane (analysis only, nothing saved or copied):\n  - OpenCritic media pages (cookie banner: \"Reject all\" in its settings): CoD: WWII\n    https://img.opencritic.com/game/4505/o/{qmtcJEVe,QkM512CZ,2I9pyxbS}.jpg (1920x1080: Sherman +\n    infantry, burning wreck, chateau, strong DOF; snowy forest firefight, fog depth, big muzzle\n    flame, fires in the haze; bunker interior: FP gloved hands on a worn MG, ceiling lamp cone in\n    dusty air, breach to a bright exterior). CoD: Vanguard\n    https://img.opencritic.com/game/12073/o/{nFJI29Tg,8T8BsLvS,QuBxN763,cGrCPR59}.jpg (3840x2160,\n    cinematic character close-ups - out of this branch's scope).\n  - CoD: WWII Carentan trailer thumbnail https://img.youtube.com/vi/3dvJxuBgoIc/maxresdefault.jpg\n    (Normandy street wall: plaster gone to brick, bullet pocks, big painted German name across the\n    building, a German direction post crowded with arrow boards, flamethrower jet lighting the wall).\n  - MoH: Airborne https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/MOHA_street.png (re-checked: dusk\n    stone street, white cloth from an arch, sandbags).\n- d3b2687c painted direction posts (signs.js): the blank 'signpost' model (two white boards) is no\n  longer drawn (levelBuild keeps its collider, returns built.signposts {x,y,z,yaw}); signs.js\n  builds post + 5-8 ExtrudeGeometry boards per post (arrow or plain plate centred on the post),\n  canvas atlas 1024x1008 (512x96 cells, 2x10, wood strip under), back face mirrored so both read,\n  text condensed to fit (DIN Condensed/Arial Narrow stack), chipped/streaked/shot. Material via\n  matlib.resolve (needs a color attribute: resolve sets vertexColors). Boards chosen by the post's\n  position (POSTS[].at within 3 m); compass N/S/E/W snapped to the post's faces. New post in the\n  square under the lamp by the church: P('signpost', -11.2, 151.8, 90) in saint-clair.js.\n- 7dbc8488 cobbles: tools/textures.py cobble() - flat worn tops (smoothstep(0,7px)^0.6 edge,\n  slight crown), per-sett tilt (cells 240/241, +-0.125 height across a stone) so wet reflections\n  break up per stone, tops rougher->smoother (0.34). Regenerated cobble.webp/cobble_n.webp (old ones\n  kept in the scratchpad tex_before/). Terrain shader untouched. A/B: the \"bubble wrap\" sparkle\n  becomes a continuous wet sheen; mean height rose 131->172 (POM shallower; joints narrow).\n- 511e29af German painted sign: atmosphere.js ADS[3] ÉPICERIE -> ORTSKOMMANDANTUR / EINGANG IM HOF\n  (black sans capitals on whitewash - the 1941 Normalschrifterlass ended Fraktur on official signs;\n  `age` 0.55 weathers it less). damage.js puts variant 3 on the cafe's south gable in the square\n  (17.8, 5.7, 153). The decal system is fixed at 4 variants per kind, hence the swap.\n  Remaining gaps seen against the references: fire definition (crisp flame tongues + a dark smoke\n  column over the burning truck - ours reads as a glow in a dense orange haze, by design so far);\n  interior lamp light cones with dust; wall base-material fidelity (assets).\nEOF\ntail -4 \"$N\"","description":"Record this turn's references and commits in the notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2415,"cache_read_input_tokens":505961,"output_tokens":2404,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":846},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_