{"parentUuid":"9bd59783-0006-4d04-a553-8eea64f1dbb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGPoDmh4v8Frv7uAH2ht","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4udc74JjkHwaawdo5B2Nd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/lights.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/mission.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: let the fires' flames stand out of their glow\n\nIn the CoD: WWII frames checked this turn, fire reads as crisp,\nlicking tongues of flame. Our burning truck read as a glow in an\norange fog. Toggling the effects one at a time showed why: the fire's\nlight, at intensity 22 over 18 m, scattered fully in the wet air. That\nmade a haze brighter than the flames and washed out the street around\nthem. With the volumetric pass off, the flame tongues were already\nthere.\n\nA fire still lights the walls, the cobbles and the soldiers in full, but\nonly 35% of its light now hangs in the air (FIRE_FOG). This applies to\nthe burning truck, the ruin, and the flak gun once it is blown. The\nflames read as tongues over the cab, the street keeps its depth beyond\nthem, and the smoke column shows against a darker sky.\n\nStatic lights could not pass a fog factor before: addStatic dropped it,\nand the shadow-casting light that leads the list ignored it. Both now\ncarry it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; REDACTED; cp $S/split_final/lights.js $S/split_final/volumetric.js $S/split_final/levelBuild.js $S/split_final/mission.js fun/hedgerow/js/ && cd fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and\n    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth) · `taa.js`\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and\n    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth; under a\n    capped lamp — the street lamps, the lanterns on the houses — only the\n    air below the cap is lit, and brighter for what the cap throws back\n    down: a bell of light in the rain, dark above it, each view ray's\n    stretch through it taken in six pieces) · `taa.js`\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass diff --stat","description":"Commit the fire change and restore the lamp cones on top"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":585470,"output_tokens":1057,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":585470,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W4udc74JjkHwaawdo5B2Nd":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/lights.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/mission.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: let the fires' flames stand out of their glow\n\nIn the CoD: WWII frames checked this turn, fire reads as crisp,\nlicking tongues of flame. Our burning truck read as a glow in an\norange fog. Toggling the effects one at a time showed why: the fire's\nlight, at intensity 22 over 18 m, scattered fully in the wet air. That\nmade a haze brighter than the flames and washed out the street around\nthem. With the volumetric pass off, the flame tongues were already\nthere.\n\nA fire still lights the walls, the cobbles and the soldiers in full, but\nonly 35% of its light now hangs in the air (FIRE_FOG). This applies to\nthe burning truck, the ruin, and the flak gun once it is blown. The\nflames read as tongues over the cab, the street keeps its depth beyond\nthem, and the smoke column shows against a darker sky.\n\nStatic lights could not pass a fog factor before: addStatic dropped it,\nand the shadow-casting light that leads the list ignored it. Both now\ncarry it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; REDACTED; cp $S/split_final/lights.js $S/split_final/volumetric.js $S/split_final/levelBuild.js $S/split_final/mission.js fun/hedgerow/js/ && cd fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and\n    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth) · `taa.js`\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and\n    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth; under a\n    capped lamp — the street lamps, the lanterns on the houses — only the\n    air below the cap is lit, and brighter for what the cap throws back\n    down: a bell of light in the rain, dark above it, each view ray's\n    stretch through it taken in six pieces) · `taa.js`\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass diff --stat","description":"Commit the fire change and restore the lamp cones on top"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d706a13c-e9bb-44d8-b77d-8f2404b35aa0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGPoDEwZYKDhz3CuHk82","requestRef":"778933de-7ee7-474b-ac56-b1472d083bef","requestedModel