:"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"6b20d330-75c3-4da2-9ca3-6e1ae951d421","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>11070571 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c3532981-c934-489d-af99-34ced7756988","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:24:47.420Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>11070571 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"162cd2f14d73f9bd43b029cd37cce7a7b0fbc7d4e1b4c7de250076feab00029a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ve2bXGkjTeYzXyUPRNgXP7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    fires as flame: three billboards per near fire, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core), `plumes.js` (each\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    fires as flame: five billboards over the breadth of each near fire,\n    rising two to three metres out of the wreck, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core), `plumes.js` (each\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/flames.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the burning truck's fire stands up out of the wreck\n\nThe CoD: WWII frames checked this turn (the wreck in the tank shot, the\nbig fire in the zombies reveal) show fire as a large body of flame that\ndominates its corner of the frame. Our truck's flames rose about half a\nmetre over the cab.\n\nflames.js now draws five flame billboards per near fire instead of\nthree, spread over the fire's breadth. They are taller (1.8-2.9 x the\nfire's size, about 2.0-3.2 m on the truck) and a little wider, and rise\nfrom a little deeper inside the wreck. The truck now reads as a burning\nvehicle from mid-street: several tongues standing well over the cab.\nThe cost is two more instanced quads per fire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; cd fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it; the fires' embers\n    carried off on the wind for seconds, swirling in its eddies as they\n    cool; a blast flashes\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it; the fires' embers\n    carried off on the wind for seconds, swirling in its eddies as they\n    cool, and every few seconds a shower of sparks spat up out of the\n    flames, arcing over and falling back; a blast flashes\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: fires throw showers of sparks\n\nThe CoD: WWII wreck fire checked this turn is full of sparks and burning\nbits. Ours sent up about seven embers a second.\n\neffects.js now gives each fire:\n- steady embers twice as often (about 15 a second), still carried off\n  on the wind and swirling as they cool;\n- every 1.5-4.5 s, a shower of 14-25 bright sparks spat up out of the\n  flames (3.5-7.5 m/s), arcing over under gravity and dying in one to\n  two seconds, as when a beam falls in or the last of the fuel catches.\n\nDistant fires do neither. Checked as a five-second sequence by the\ntruck: about 620-700 particles alive in all, well within the systems'\ncapacity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2; git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merge-tree: clean\" || echo \"merge-tree: conflicts ($?)\"; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the bigger flames and the sparks separately"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
