{"parentUuid":"549d580a-f5b6-41a7-8062-057700231fcf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGQrrsL5EN2cXnLf9GWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I closed the fire gap the last review named: the CoD fires were bigger and threw more sparks than our truck. I re-checked the CoD: WWII wreck fire up close: a large body of flame, dozens of sparks and burning bits around it and on the ground, dark smoke above. I added each missing element in turn, with one commit each:\n\n- **e1b9a715, flames.** Each fire now has five flame layers spread across it instead of three, taller and wider. On the truck the flames stand about 1.5 m over the cab instead of half a metre.\n- **fa8fe595, sparks.** Twice as many steady embers. Every few seconds each fire also spits a shower of 14–25 sparks that arc up and fall back, as when a beam falls in.\n- **f9d442ba, smoke.** The fire's own smoke is twice as dense, darker and bigger. A dark mass now rolls up from the flame tips into the existing smoke plume. From down the street it reads as a dark column against the orange-lit air.\n- **6f9f7795, burning debris.** Small fires now burn on the cobbles around the truck (four) and the halftrack by the bridge (three), with flames, sparks and smoke to their size. They're kept in a separate list, so they can't push the real fires out of the smoke plumes, the heat haze, the glowing charred wood or the fire glow on the clouds.\n\nAll three quality presets compile with the fires in view. The 9 node checks pass, and each commit merges cleanly with hedgerow-poc. Nothing is pushed.\n\nThe whole truck fire now costs about 2 ms of GPU time when seen from 6 m on high quality. That's the worst case, with the fire filling the view. The large dark smoke particles are the most likely bulk, so that's where to trim if frame rate gets tight.\n\nThe shared notes have the details and that cost figure. The test browser and server are stopped, and my `launch.json` entry is removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":667890,"output_tokens":629,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":667890,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"39f74cd6-bce0-4b25-8c1c-62d12ebb9e9a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGQrrFcJus1WeAVke7hE","requestRef":"c68f7b08-28ab-4b76-a30c-492076a1f168","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"0b02e2a4-bd4b-4235-90e6-1456045fb6ba","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:31:47.016Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
