{"parentUuid":"78b2e6c1-f754-40b3-b19c-27eccdebddef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGR26oEebu4Tu8aiBpxs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since the sync tool only pulls from `origin` and would miss `hedgerow-poc`'s local-only commits, I'll merge `refs/heads/hedgerow-poc` myself—its changes are confined to `fun/hedgerow`, so no protected files are touched. First I'll check a new memory about verifying headlessly, since it affects how I'll validate the merge.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":678966,"output_tokens":1142,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1142,"cache_read_input_tokens":678966,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a93e1158-34cd-496c-beaa-0d8bdae9f326","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGR25rAww3e3dpjPk466","requestRef":"44166e59-1c7d-48bd-89cc-c35dd19c7a7a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d814512-fd5b-489f-a216-0831364076c5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:33:58.110Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"6d814512-fd5b-489f-a216-0831364076c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGR26oEebu4Tu8aiBpxs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016BEwTGp9wGTmuQ7qKFFZF1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/verify-headlessly.md; echo ----; cat /Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/close-test-browsers.md","description":"Read the two memory rules about testing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":678966,"output_tokens":1142,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1142,"cache_read_input_tokens":678966,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016BEwTGp9wGTmuQ7qKFFZF1":{"command":"cat /Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/verify-headlessly.md; echo ----; cat /Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/close-test-browsers.md","description":"Read the two memory rules about testing"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a93e1158-34cd-496c-beaa-0d8bdae9f326","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGR25rAww3e3dpjPk466","requestRef":"44166e59-1c7d-48bd-89cc-c35dd19c7a7a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e48131ec-de81-4531-be74-b57f4833b31b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:33:58.113Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"e48131ec-de81-4531-be74-b57f4833b31b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016BEwTGp9wGTmuQ7qKFFZF1","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: verify-headlessly\ndescription: \"Don't open the built-in browser pane for game checks; the user closes it — verify with headless Node checks instead\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d\n  modified: 2026-10-21T13:08:58.895Z\n---\n\nWhen working on the protocodus games (Hedgerow in fun/hedgerow), don't reopen the built-in browser pane (preview_start / navigate) for visual checks once the user has closed it. On 2026-10-21 the user closed the pane twice in a row mid-test and stopped the test server; they play the builds themselves and report what they see (e.g. \"the weapon bobs too much\").\n\n**Why:** The pane takes over their screen while they are playing or watching; closing it is their answer.\n\n**How to apply:** Verify with Node checks against the real assets (fun/hedgerow/tests/*.mjs load the GLBs with textures stripped, e.g. tests/fp-check.mjs measures first-person weapon sway and sight alignment) and say plainly in the report which visuals were not seen in a browser. If a look truly needs eyes, ask first. Still close anything that was opened ([[close-test-browsers]]).\n----\n---\nname: close-test-browsers\ndescription: \"Always close every browser session (Playwright, built-in browser pane, Chrome tabs) and local test server after using it for testing\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: a284be7e-0c21-492c-a5ea-79db742276fc\n  modified: 2026-10-13T07:51:55.230Z\n---\n\nAlways end all browser sessions used for testing — Playwright MCP browsers (browser_close), built-in browser pane tabs (tabs_close), Chrome tabs opened for the test — and stop any local static server started to serve the page, as soon as the test is done. Don't leave them running between tests or at the end of a turn.\n\n**Why:** The user asked for it explicitly (2026-10-13, while testing the Meteora game in fun/meteora); leftover headless browsers and servers pile up across a long session.\n\n**How to apply:** After each visual check, close the browser/tab in the same step sequence; at the end of a task, verify nothing is left (e.g. `ps -axo pid,command | grep -i playwright`, `lsof -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN`).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ba25154d-60da-4b2f-acac-eac7dd4237b2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:33:58.620Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: verify-headlessly\ndescription: \"Don't open the built-in browser pane for game checks; the user closes it — verify with headless Node checks instead\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d\n  modified: 2026-10-21T13:08:58.895Z\n---\n\nWhen working on the protocodus games (Hedgerow in fun/hedgerow), don't reopen the built-in browser pane (preview_start / navigate) for visual checks once the user has closed it. On 2026-10-21 the user closed the pane twice in a row mid-test and stopped the test server; they play the builds themselves and report what they see (e.g. \"the weapon bobs too much\").\n\n**Why:** The pane takes over their screen while they are playing or watching; closing it is their answer.\n\n**How to apply:** Verify with Node checks against the real assets (fun/hedgerow/tests/*.mjs load the GLBs with textures stripped, e.g. tests/fp-check.mjs measures first-person weapon sway and sight alignment) and say plainly in the report which visuals were not seen in a browser. If a look truly needs eyes, ask first. Still close anything that was opened ([[close-test-browsers]]).\n----\n---\nname: close-test-browsers\ndescription: \"Always close every browser session (Playwright, built-in browser pane, Chrome tabs) and local test server after using it for testing\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: a284be7e-0c21-492c-a5ea-79db742276fc\n  modified: 2026-10-13T07:51:55.230Z\n---\n\nAlways end all browser sessions used for testing — Playwright MCP browsers (browser_close), built-in browser pane tabs (tabs_close), Chrome tabs opened for the test — and stop any local static server started to serve the page, as soon as the test is done. Don't leave them running between tests or at the end of a turn.\n\n**Why:** The user asked for it explicitly (2026-10-13, while testing the Meteora game in fun/meteora); leftover headless browsers and servers pile up across a long session.\n\n**How to apply:** After each visual check, close the browser/tab in the same step sequence; at the end of a task, verify nothing is left (e.g. `ps -axo pid,command | grep -i playwright`, `lsof -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a93e1158-34cd-496c-beaa-0d8bdae9f326","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e48131ec-de81-4531-be74-b57f4833b31b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cla