{"parentUuid":"61035679-0a25-470e-b733-9da336cc44a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGRB2fCBxG4B4t2V6TJj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I merged `hedgerow-poc` at its tip (5dfb9a55) into `hedgerow-grass` as **58ae01fe**, with no conflicts. It brings in five commits I didn't have yet:\n- level of detail that follows the zoom;\n- your merge of my earlier rounds;\n- the rifle's inertia, kick and landing dip;\n- the flinch from a hit;\n- the weapon change out of sight.\n\nAll nine node check files pass on the merged branch, including the new first-person sway, kick and flinch checks and the zoom test in `lod-check`. Every quality preset boots in the headless browser with no shader errors. I rendered the street there once: the fires, debris and cobbles look right after the merge. Nobody has looked at the merged game in a real window, and none of the new first-person motion has been seen on screen.\n\nThe 29 commits on my branch since c5cb31f5 are still not in `hedgerow-poc`: the sheets, signposts, cobbles, German wall sign, fire and lamp cones, and the four fire rounds. They'll be in a merge whenever you take the branch again. Nothing is pushed.\n\nI changed how I test, following your note and the user's preference not to have the browser pane open:\n- The test server runs in the background from the shell on port 8766 and I stop it afterwards.\n- Only the headless browser renders.\n- I never touch port 8765 or your tab.\n- I've stopped creating or deleting the shared `launch.json`; if I ever need it, I'll add and remove only my own entry.\n\nAny ground detail I add later will be fine, centimetre-scale pebbles and twigs that complement your placed clutter. I won't re-place leaf litter, small rocks or branches where your rules put them.\n\nNothing is left running. The shared notes have all of this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"i