{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"2333a6f83af804c7d269016b91c2d6fed96f1443e810b686e526eea97bdd0938","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The review asks for a sustained loop toward AAA parity, so I'll keep the rig up and make several improvements this turn, each checked against reference frames. Verification stays headless, per the user's preference.\n\nOne telling difference between our captures and the CoD frames is how buildings meet the ground. CoD walls darken toward their feet with damp and rain splashback, and grime streaks run down from the sills. Our walls look evenly clean from roof to ground, as if set on top of the street. First I'm checking what the wall shader already does near the ground."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EEgEUHdHhRZzp1rLET9AWw","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Check wall-base wetness, pick round's improvements","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Rising damp and splashback at wall bases","status":"pending"},{"content":"Warm bounce light round fires","status":"pending"},{"content":"Verify presets and node checks, commit each","status":"pending"},{"content":"Re-compare to references, notes, shut down","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R4YLS9dj46LAKF3JYfW3K2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n -i \"damp\\|splash\\|base of\\|near the ground\\|ground height\\|GROUND_GLSL\\|uMapMin\\|tGround\" js/materials.js | head -20; grep -n \"export const GROUND_GLSL\" -A30 js/groundmap.js | head -45","description":"Check for existing wall-base wetness and the ground height map"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
