{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"ceea8a026449ee69d9b73e687bef3a938f954c3be9c916f1d21880ec1cfef749","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016gfjgEsQCTWpoyXVwg1YZp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\n    `lightloop.js` (three.js shades\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it; and\n    the fires' light thrown back off the street and the walls round them,\n    the four nearest: a warm fill, unshadowed, on what stands within ~20 m\n    of a fire, most on the side facing it, a third on its sides, little on\n    the side turned away, so a wreck's shadow side and the street behind\n    it are not black and a wall round a fire is not lit through),\n    `lightloop.js` (three.js shades\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/fill.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: fires throw warm light back off their surroundings\n\nIn the CoD frames, a fire warms everything round it, including what its\nflames don't reach directly: light bounced off the lit street and walls.\nOurs lit only what its shadowed point light hit, so a wreck's shadow\nside and the street behind it stayed black.\n\nfill.js addFireBounce adds a warm, unshadowed fill to the indirect light\nof every weather-patched material and of the terrain, from the four\nnearest fires:\n- it falls off with distance and is gone by 20 m;\n- it lights most the side facing the flames, a third the sides, and\n  little the side turned away, so a wall round a fire is not lit\n  through.\n\nThe ruin's fire burns inside its walls, and the first version warmed its\nouter façade; that was the reason for the facing cut. The fires' uniform\n(FIRE_UNIFORMS) moved to fill.js so the terrain can share it without an\nimport cycle, and the smouldering char still reads it as before.\n\nMeasured with the flicker held still: the frame's darker half is 2.2-2.8\ngrey levels brighter round the truck, the ruin and the halftrack\n(+7-15%), with no orange wash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merge-tree: clean\" || echo \"merge-tree: conflicts ($?)\"; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the fire bounce light and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
