{"parentUuid":"b97b8431-db2c-4ec2-a73d-91c273f58d66","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGSBpowZu36J611dJRzS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two more improvements this round, each closing a gap against the CoD frames:\n\n- **c597cb3d, damp at the foot of walls.** In the CoD Carentan frame, the wall darkens and dirties toward the ground. Ours were evenly clean down to the cobbles. Now every wall, step, crate, barrel and sandbag gets:\n  - a ragged band of rising damp 35–85 cm high, darker and slightly green on stone and plaster;\n  - a faint tide line where the damp stops;\n  - mud splashed up in specks near the ground.\n\n  My first strength was invisible at night, so I strengthened it, and a debug colouring confirmed the band sits where it should.\n- **dd358324, warm bounce light from fires.** In the CoD fires, the surroundings glow warm even where the flames don't reach directly. Ours stayed black in the fire's shadow. The four nearest fires now add a warm, unshadowed fill to everything within about 20 m, including the ground, strongest on the side facing the flames. My first version lit the ruin's outside wall through the wall from the fire inside, so surfaces facing away now get very little. With the fires' flicker held still, the darker half of the frame near the fires comes out 7–15% brighter, without an orange wash.\n\nAll three quality presets compile with no failed shaders, the 9 node checks pass, and both commits merge cleanly with hedgerow-poc. Nothing is pushed. I checked everything only in headless renders; nobody has seen either change in a real browser window.\n\nThe test server and headless browser are stopped; the browser pane was never opened. The details are in the shared notes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":776561,"output_tokens":532,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":776561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1405b5af-09f8-4e8c-ab4c-e0003246db3d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGSBpExw2FrgZPL34ABa","requestRef":"dd6c42df-c106-46ec-a066-e06d511795b1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"56e37bed-07e9-41ee-9378-6741efa91e7f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:49:10.505Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
