{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"2b26a3220191d7dcf045d5060d5d2e936985b72e3ad5e6301044d928b03f4e53","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hook will keep asking for more, which matches the user's goal, so I'll keep improving each turn. Teardown at turn end stays: the user's own rule asks for it, and also for keeping the browser pane closed, which is why changes are checked headless rather than in a window.\n\nFor this round I'm looking for the next most visible difference. One stands out in our captures: unlit window glass is flat black. In a wet night street, glass reflects the lamps, the fires and the glow of the sky, and the reference frames' windows catch light the same way. Checking how window glass is set up in the materials."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019f5UX1gUhhiUTbKbSv7e5y","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Find how unlit window glass is shaded","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Make dark window glass reflect the night","status":"pending"},{"content":"Verify presets and node checks, commit","status":"pending"},{"content":"Next improvement from the comparison","status":"pending"},{"content":"Notes and shut down the rig","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WMbd2NCzb56qEuzFeoHviG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n -i \"glass\\|window\\|pane\" js/materials.js | head -20; grep -n -i \"glass\\|window\" assets/models/MODELS.md | head -20","description":"Find any glass or window materials in the game"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"0591788aacbf6ab8c63c46fbbdccc7c1f80aaf59fd00ec765a2f606ee7eb177c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019f5UX1gUhhiUTbKbSv7e5y","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (5 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMbd2NCzb56qEuzFeoHviG","type":"tool_result","content":"32:  glass: ['metal', 1.0, 0.1, 0.0, { roughness: 0.05, metalness: 0.0, env: 1.6 }],\n33:  window_lit: ['metal', 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, { emissive: '#ffa04a', emissiveIntensity: 2.4 }],\n83:  glass: '#151b21', window_lit: '#ffb35c', iron: '#2e2f31', rust: '#6e3b22', concrete: '#8c8a84', cobble: '#6c6862',\n94:  roof_slate: 0.6, glass: 0.1, iron: 0.5, rust: 0.8, metal_olive: 0.5, metal_gray: 0.5, metal_dark: 0.45,\n282:        // bark, what is carried or the lit panes)\n299:   window panes (rooms.js) show the room behind them. */\n706:      // the room behind the pane (instead of the baked glow), seen through old glass which\n722:          // rain beaded on the glass bends the view through it (each bead a little lens), its rim bright\n39:   blown patches, dirty glass, barrel tiles with lichen, slate,\n46:   shared ones at run time (masonry, plaster, glass and paint in","is_error":false}]}}
