{"parentUuid":"3239e00b-b144-4d57-b1e6-706421cccf92","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGSF7QRHdivndfboPd9W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M9F1Y3w2Lp7VKbfPtdgq2T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 30,60p assets/models/MODELS.md","description":"Read how the models' glass and textures are described"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3625,"cache_read_input_tokens":777687,"output_tokens":149,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3625,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":149,"cache_read_input_tokens":777687,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3625,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3625},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01M9F1Y3w2Lp7VKbfPtdgq2T":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && sed -n 30,60p assets/models/MODELS.md","description":"Read how the models' glass and textures are described"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01M9F1Y3w2Lp7VKbfPtdgq2T":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"57601ba3-4490-42d6-b3c6-7d3edef69416","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGSF6pCtN82hM9xGL1xZ","requestRef":"822adfe0-bcb2-416d-b06b-0a8f9878917e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"b436c635-6eac-4b55-8a2a-8fe1c2c176c4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:49:51.611Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"b436c635-6eac-4b55-8a2a-8fe1c2c176c4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M9F1Y3w2Lp7VKbfPtdgq2T","type":"tool_result","content":"## How a model is made\n\n1. Geometry from bmesh primitives and lofts in the build script, each part\n   given a **palette key** material (`kit.PALETTE`).\n2. `bake.bake_model()` unwraps an atlas, bakes ambient occlusion (with a\n   ground plane) and an edge mask, swaps every palette key for its\n   procedural surface from `surfaces.py` (coursed rubble with washed-out\n   lime mortar, Caen-stone dressings, plaster with cracks, run-off and\n   blown patches, dirty glass, barrel tiles with lichen, slate,\n   planks, peeling paint, chipped and rusted paint on steel, blued steel,\n   board-formed concrete, hessian, wool, leather, skin, bark, granite...)\n   plus shared weathering (occlusion, cavity dirt, splash at the base, rain\n   streaks, moss, worn edges), then bakes base colour, roughness, metallic,\n   emission and a tangent-space normal (bevelled edges + bump).\n   The village and military builds register their own recipes over the\n   shared ones at run time (masonry, plaster, glass and paint in\n   `village_parts.py`; rust and grime drip maps, mud, board-formed concrete,\n   hessian and tyre rubber in `military_parts.py`).\n3. One material per node; WebP textures inside the GLB\n   (`EXT_texture_webp`, which three.js r185's `GLTFLoader` reads).\n4. Foliage, ivy and the camouflage net are alpha cards (glTF alphaMode\n   MASK) on atlases rendered in Blender from modelled leaves, needles and\n   blades; the game draws them double-sided with the alpha test, lit from\n   the card normals, swaying in the wind.\n\nThe game replaces nothing in a baked material; it only adds the rain\n(darker porous surfaces, glossier everything, water film and ripples on\nupward faces) in `js/materials.js`.\n\nReview renders go to `tools/blender/previews/<set>/` (hundreds of MB, not","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5312ba90-f57a-4838-bbd3-756ccda1ecce","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:49:52.065Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## How a model is made\n\n1. Geometry from bmesh primitives and lofts in the build script, each part\n   given a **palette key** material (`kit.PALETTE`).\n2. `bake.bake_model()` unwraps an atlas, bakes ambient occlusion (with a\n   ground plane) and an edge mask, swaps every palette key for its\n   procedural surface from `surfaces.py` (coursed rubble with washed-out\n   lime mortar, Caen-stone dressings, plaster with cracks, run-off and\n   blown patches, dirty glass, barrel tiles with lichen, slate,\n   planks, peeling paint, chipped and rusted paint on steel, blued steel,\n   board-formed concrete, hessian, wool, leather, skin, bark, granite...)\n   plus shared weathering (occlusion, cavity dirt, splash at the base, rain\n   streaks, moss, worn edges), then bakes base colour, roughness, metallic,\n   emission and a tangent-space normal (bevelled edges + bump).\n   The village and military builds register their own recipes over the\n   shared ones at run time (masonry, plaster, glass and paint in\n   `village_parts.py`; rust and grime drip maps, mud, board-formed concrete,\n   hessian and tyre rubber in `military_parts.py`).\n3. One material per node; WebP textures inside the GLB\n   (`EXT_texture_webp`, which three.js r185's `GLTFLoader` reads).\n4. Foliage, ivy and the camouflage net are alpha cards (glTF alphaMode\n   MASK) on atlases rendered in Blender from modelled leaves, needles and\n   blades; the game draws them double-sided with the alpha test, lit from\n   the card normals, swaying in the wind.\n\nThe game replaces nothing in a baked material; it only adds the rain\n(darker porous surfaces, glossier everything, water film and ripples on\nupward faces) in `js/materials.js`.\n\nReview renders go to `tools/blender/previews/<set>/` (hundreds of MB, not","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"57601ba3-4490-42d6-b3c6-7d3edef69416","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b436c635-6eac-4b55-8a2a-8fe1c2c176c4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
