{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"370b7bda8f026cdfc44f32414785f755859f63218afa49a8737c1875bf731ee3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D372U8xk1p9DMdXZjCnhHq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    rings where drops land (on the river's surface over its bed), and\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    rings where drops land - on the first thing in their way from above, a\n    crate's lid, a sandbag, a step, the truck, a roof, so what is\n    sheltered stays dry (on the river's surface over its bed) - and\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain lands on what it meets first\n\nIn heavy rain in AAA levels, drops splash on every upward surface. Ours\nlanded at terrain height only. So no splash ever showed on a crate's lid,\na sandbag, a step or the truck's bonnet, and the ones whose spot lay\nunder a prop or inside a house were drawn hidden beneath it.\n\nweather.js landY now casts each landing spot down from 30 m above it\nthrough the world's colliders (SHOT mask: walls, crates, vehicles,\nsandbags; not foliage or the invisible play-area walls). The rings and\nthe crowns of droplets stand on the first upward-facing top they meet,\nso what is sheltered under it stays dry. A hit that starts inside\nsomething tall is not taken as a top. main.js passes G.world to the\nweather.\n\nChecked: in a crop of a crate's lid, crowns and rings now appear on it.\n4400 such rays (about a second of splashes and crowns) take 0.9 ms of\nCPU, and 19% of random spots down the street land on a top, mostly\nroofs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merge-tree: clean\" || echo \"merge-tree: conflicts ($?)\"; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the rain landing change and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
