{"parentUuid":"6e05043f-ed44-4e0f-9229-ff29ead825f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGSxmkea5XTddnDrhSqL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Scenes outside the village read very dark, consistent with overall exposure—since night readability is already flagged for the user to decide on, I won't adjust exposure myself. I'll wrap up this round with notes, then shut down.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":842467,"output_tokens":1499,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":410},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":842467,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9603817b-30a5-467d-a232-ccd69508ca01","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGSxmARwzUJA7uGDj9r9","requestRef":"60079aa9-1824-4700-9af5-07078a587a95","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"701e52f6-efb7-474e-a3a2-1fc2681fe6a4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:59:22.487Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"701e52f6-efb7-474e-a3a2-1fc2681fe6a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGSxmkea5XTddnDrhSqL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011RHvAmW9pao7GgUAeZvKLu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, fifth:\n- Tried and reverted (not committed): reflections in upright window glass. Debug colouring found the\n  baked panes at wet roughness 0.16-0.24 (upright); the weather patch told ssr.js only about level\n  water (mirrorAlpha via mWetUp), and ssr.js drops non-level normals, downward rays and hits not\n  above the water. A glass range in the scene alpha (0.5-0.75, glass = upright mirror) plus ssr.js\n  and volumetric.js reading it worked technically, but A/Bs from head-on, grazing and fire-aligned\n  views showed nothing concentrated in the panes (screen space: the head-on reflection is behind the\n  camera; at grazing angles the panes mirror the dark houses opposite). Not worth the risk.\n- 87bdf2f5 rain lands on what it meets first: weather.js landY casts down from y + 30 through\n  world colliders (SHOT, noTerrain, noWater; ignore t < 0.01 = started inside), takes an upward top\n  above the ground; main.js passes world. Crowns/rings now on crate lids etc. 4400 rays = 0.9 ms CPU\n  (per second of splashes); 19% of random street spots land on a top (mostly roofs).\n- Looked at the lane, a field and the forest track: very dark - exposure/readability at night stays\n  the user's call (gap 8).\n  Not seen in a real browser window: headless renders only.\nEOF\ncd REDACTED && node hl.mjs stop; for i in $(seq 1 15); do pgrep -f chrome-headless-shell >/dev/null || break; sleep 1; done; rm -rf hl-profile; pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"; sleep 1; pgrep -fl chrome-headless-shell || echo \"no headless processes\"; pgrep -fl \"nocache_server.py\" || echo \"no test server\"; lsof -iTCP:8766 -sTCP:LISTEN >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"8766 still listening\" || echo \"8766 free\"; git -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass status --short | head -3; git -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass log --oneline -2","description":"Record the round and shut down the rig","timeout":60000,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":842467,"output_tokens":1499,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":410},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":842467,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011RHvAmW9pao7GgUAeZvKLu":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, fifth:\n- Tried and reverted (not committed): reflections in upright window glass. Debug colouring found the\n  baked panes at wet roughness 0.16-0.24 (upright); the weather patch told ssr.js only about level\n  water (mirrorAlpha via mWetUp), and ssr.js drops non-level normals, downward rays and hits not\n  above the water. A glass range in the scene alpha (0.5-0.75, glass = upright mirror) plus ssr.js\n  and volumetric.js reading it worked technically, but A/Bs from head-on, grazing and fire-aligned\n  views showed nothing concentrated in the panes (screen space: the head-on reflection is behind the\n  camera; at grazing angles the panes mirror the dark houses opposite). Not worth the risk.\n- 87bdf2f5 rain lands on what it meets first: weather.js landY casts down from y + 30 through\n  world colliders (SHOT, noTerrain, noWater; ignore t < 0.01 = started inside), takes an upward top\n  above the ground; main.js passes world. Crowns/rings now on crate lids etc. 4400 rays = 0.9 ms CPU\n  (per second of splashes); 19% of random street spots land on a top (mostly roofs).\n- Looked at the lane, a field and the forest track: very dark - exposure/readability at night stays\n  the user's call (gap 8).\n  Not seen in a real browser window: headless renders only.\nEOF\ncd REDACTED && node hl.mjs stop; for i in $(seq 1 15); do pgrep -f chrome-headless-shell >/dev/null || break; sleep 1; done; rm -rf hl-profile; pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"; sleep 1; pgrep -fl chrome-headless-shell || echo \"no headless processes\"; pgrep -fl \"nocache_server.py\" || echo \"no test server\"; lsof -iTCP:8766 -sTCP:LISTEN >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"8766 still listening\" || echo \"8766 free\"; git -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass status --short | head -3; git -C /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass log --oneline -2","description":"Record the round and shut down the rig","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":60000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9603817b-30a5-467d-a232-ccd69508ca01","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGSxmARwzUJA7uGDj9r9","requestRef":"60079aa9-1824-4700-9af5-07078a587a95","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"18cf1dc8-26c4-4c05-ad5a-43887e80dbae","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:59:30.808Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
