{"parentUuid":"8024ac15-53ca-446f-806f-87d173610ac3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGT1WirXsMrzhqfCRGLF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round I committed one improvement and reverted one that didn't pay off:\n\n- **87bdf2f5, rain lands on what it meets first.** In heavy rain in AAA levels, drops splash on every upward surface. Ours always landed at ground height, so crate lids, sandbags and steps never got splashes, and splashes under props or inside houses were hidden. Each splash and droplet crown now lands on the first solid surface beneath it, so sheltered ground stays dry. In a close-up of a crate lid, droplet crowns and rings now appear on it. The cost is about 0.02 ms of CPU per frame.\n- **Window glass reflections, reverted.** Unlit windows look flat black. The reflection system turned out to handle only level water, so I extended it to upright glass. It worked technically, but comparisons from straight-on, grazing and fire-aligned views showed nothing visible in the windows. Head-on, a window reflects what's behind the camera, which screen-based reflections can't see; at grazing angles the panes mostly mirror the dark houses opposite. It wasn't worth the added risk, so I reverted it.\n\nI also looked at the sunken lane, the fields and the forest track. They're very dark, but that comes from the overall exposure, which is already on the list as the user's call, so I left it alone.\n\nEvery preset loads, the 9 node checks pass, and the commit merges cleanly with hedgerow-poc. Nothing is pushed. I checked everything only in headless renders, not in a browser window. The test server and headless browser are stopped, and the notes record both the commit and the reverted attempt."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_read_input_tokens":845544,"output_tokens":523,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":246,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":845544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":246},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"31861714-a48c-4e15-902e-b7c480e11b5a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGT1VxiS3R6kwwGD9ZGd","requestRef":"d8c5d907-5747-4a57-8eb4-8a31e7accc76","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"e81f6a83-2dd3-444c-9cc3-8333cdef9ff4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:59:57.381Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
