{"parentUuid":"09199b51-2ad3-445f-89d1-9d6e05f04ff2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGTsaJYumB6wb4dcQUBq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every preset compiles with the wire's program running, and all nine check files pass. Adding `wire.js` to the README and committing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":907826,"output_tokens":1233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1233,"cache_read_input_tokens":907826,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"75833987-60fd-4f51-894f-d90185222530","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGTsZ3tHfJYE3tB6hpvK","requestRef":"bdbba906-3b47-4829-b0a1-2729852ddfc1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"acdc5bf8-a0b7-4578-9a95-05ac6041ac1b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:11:12.510Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"acdc5bf8-a0b7-4578-9a95-05ac6041ac1b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGTsaJYumB6wb4dcQUBq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ETBwxuF6uHEgjjT24iMiCY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    levelBuild keeps the signpost model's collider and leaves the drawing\n    to it),\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    levelBuild keeps the signpost model's collider and leaves the drawing\n    to it), `wire.js` (a coil of concertina along every barbed-wire\n    obstacle: loops of weathered galvanised wire some 85 cm across, each a\n    little different, leaning one way and the next the other where they\n    were clipped together so they cross in the diamonds of concertina,\n    sagging, wet and catching a lamp or a flare in glints; one mesh, the\n    wire widened in its vertex shader so it is never thinner than about a\n    pixel - a tangle from afar, wire close by),\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: concertina wire along the barbed-wire obstacles\n\nThe Medal of Honor: Airborne Neptune frames checked this turn (via the\nvideo thumbnails, in the headless browser) are full of barbed wire:\ncoils and entanglements that read clearly. Ours were knife rests strung\nwith a few strands that vanish beyond a couple of metres.\n\nwire.js lays a coil of concertina along each barbed_wire obstacle:\n- loops of about 85 cm, each a little different, sagging and leaning;\n- successive loops tilted alternately about the vertical, so they cross\n  in the diamonds of real concertina rather than reading as a spring;\n- wet, weathered galvanised steel (#8a8378, metalness 0.45, roughness\n  0.36);\n- a vertex shader that widens the 2.8 mm wire to at least about a pixel\n  on screen.\n\nIt is one mesh (22k vertices, 44k triangles) with no shadow casting.\nlevelBuild passes each obstacle's placement and length, read from the\nmodel's box.\n\nGetting it to show took three fixes. The tube was first wound inside\nout, so only its far, unlit inner side drew. A dark rust brown matched\nthe night ground. Then a white test showed an even helix reads as a\ntoy spring, which the alternating tilt fixes. Up close by a lantern the\ncoil now reads as concertina; from 3-4 m in the dark forest it is a\nfaint tangle, as wire at night should be.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merge-tree: clean\" || echo \"merge-tree: conflicts ($?)\"; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the concertina wire and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":907826,"output_tokens":1233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1233,"cache_read_input_tokens":907826,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ETBwxuF6uHEgjjT24iMiCY":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    levelBuild keeps the signpost model's collider and leaves the drawing\n    to it),\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    levelBuild keeps the signpost model's collider and leaves the drawing\n    to it), `wire.js` (a coil of concertina along every barbed-wire\n    obstacle: loops of weathered galvanised wire some 85 cm across, each a\n    little different, leaning one way and the next the other where they\n    were clipped together so they cross in the diamonds of concertina,\n    sagging, wet and catching a lamp or a flare in glints; one mesh, the\n    wire widened in its vertex shader so it is never thinner than about a\n    pixel - a tangle from afar, wire close by),\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: concertina wire along the barbed-wire obstacles\n\nThe Medal of Honor: Airborne Neptune frames checked this turn (via the\nvideo thumbnails, in the headless browser) are full of barbed wire:\ncoils and entanglements that read clearly. Ours were knife rests strung\nwith a few strands that vanish beyond a couple of metres.\n\nwire.js lays a coil of concertina along each barbed_wire obstacle:\n- loops of about 85 cm, each a little different, sagging and leaning;\n- successive loops tilted alternately about the vertical, so they cross\n  in the diamonds of real concertina rather than reading as a spring;\n- wet, weathered galvanised steel (#8a8378, metalness 0.45, roughness\n  0.36);\n- a vertex shader that widens the 2.8 mm wire to at least about a pixel\n  on screen.\n\nIt is one mesh (22k vertices, 44k triangles) with no shadow casting.\nlevelBuild passes each obstacle's placement and length, read from the\nmodel's box.\n\nGetting it to show took three fixes. The tube was first wound inside\nout, so only its far, unlit inner side drew. A dark rust brown matched\nthe night ground. Then a white test showed an even helix reads as a\ntoy spring, which the alternating tilt fixes. Up close by a lantern the\ncoil now reads as concertina; from 3-4 m in the dark forest it is a\nfaint tangle, as wire at night should be.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merge-tree: clean\" || echo \"merge-tree: conflicts ($?)\"; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the concertina wire and check the merge"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"75833987-60fd-4f51-894f-d90185222530","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGTsZ3tHfJYE3tB6hpvK","requestRef":"bdbba906-3b47-4829-b0a1-2729852ddfc1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2b2eea3-5b41-4dec-a1fa-c356c3fa77fa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:11:22.454Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
