{"parentUuid":"bab1734d-38b2-4ac3-bb0e-4dff9c98d22d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGTwCawywN5gKbssFkXD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round's improvement is **fd184b5e: concertina wire along the barbed-wire obstacles.**\n\nI compared against new references: real frames from Medal of Honor: Airborne's Normandy mission (Operation Neptune). I viewed them as video thumbnails in the headless browser; the browser pane stayed closed. Its trenches are full of coiled concertina wire that reads clearly. Ours had wooden trestles with a few thin strands that vanished beyond a couple of metres.\n\nEvery barbed-wire obstacle now has a coil of wet, weathered steel wire along it, about 85 cm across. Neighbouring loops lean alternately, so they cross in concertina's diamond pattern instead of looking like a spring. The wire is widened on screen at a distance so it doesn't flicker away. Up close by a lantern it reads clearly as concertina; from 3–4 m in the dark forest it's a faint tangle, as wire at night should be.\n\nIt took three fixes to get there:\n- The tube was first built inside out, so only its unlit inner side drew.\n- A rust brown matched the dark ground exactly.\n- A white test showed a plain coil looks like a toy spring, which the alternating lean fixes.\n\nAll three quality presets compile, the 9 node checks pass, and the commit merges cleanly with hedgerow-poc. Nothing is pushed. I checked it only in headless renders, not in a browser window. The test server and headless browser are stopped, and I deleted the reference screenshots once I'd finished comparing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":913462,"output_tokens":499,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":913462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":323},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e5449a25-a73c-4f25-82e0-c67ff1760509","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGTwBq3oqaR1PB4c9znr","requestRef":"cc968fab-7d8e-4581-aa00-d02e6f7b130b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"af584803-7f65-4b9c-b04a-a8e1e6695637","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:12:05.033Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"af584803-7f65-4b9c-b04a-a8e1e6695637","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Stop hook feedback:\n[constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards aaa game (call of duty, medal of honor). commit each improvement.]: The commit clause is satisfied: many 'Hedgerow graphics' commits exist, most recently fd184b5e. The open-ended clause, constantly and iteratively improving toward AAA (Call of Duty / Medal of Honor) quality, is not satisfied. The transcript shows discrete rounds that each end in teardown, with no completed match to AAA parity. The last message says the work was checked only in headless renders and that nothing is pushed, and the comparisons rest on a few reference frames and self-judged gaps. The assistant itself reported that its window-glass attempt produced no visible gain and was reverted."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"04f34777-8a99-4a71-abdb-a3d46b94aa11","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:12:12.048Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
