{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"e5641aae843866dd24a648d6f44e1ee87498565df88c74f8d97655ce9a9dbf5e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll build a `bootPrint` painter with alternating left/right hobnailed soles (scuffed and water-filled variants), pinned to muddy room tiles along the soldiers' routes, using an explicit heading in `pin()`. Next I'll check the route lines' format and the terrain's surface lookup to place them correctly.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TSsu7UgPEaYLuuGJdu946J","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"export function smoothPolyline\" -A12 js/util.js | head -16; grep -n \"surfaceAt\" js/terrain.js | head -3; grep -n \"function surfaceAt\" -A6 js/terrain.js | head -10; grep -n \"LEVEL.lines\" js/main.js | head -3","description":"Read the polyline format and the surface lookup"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
