{"parentUuid":"9af694bb-4948-4a31-b1fd-5b9ab34325a4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, SendMessage, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__find, mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__read_console_messages, mcp__Claude_Browser__resize_window, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_close, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context, mcp__ccd_session__hand_off_to_session, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Context.** This is a side session started by `local_7d29cad9-bdd3-4987-9ed1-e8d4d12a5721` (\"WW2 arcade 3D shooter POC\").\n     - Game: Hedgerow (`fun/hedgerow`, three.js r185, no build step).\n     - Worktree: `/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass`, branch `hedgerow-grass`.\n   - **Standing goal**, enforced by a Stop hook that re-prompts after every turn: \"constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards aaa game (call of duty, medal of honor). commit each improvement.\"\n     - The hook always says the commit clause is met but the open-ended clause is not.\n     - Its criticisms: rounds end in teardown; comparisons rest on few frames and self-judged gaps; checks are headless-only; nothing is pushed; no AAA parity.\n     - Latest: \"Iteration is ongoing, so the condition is not yet satisfied.\"\n     - The approach is to keep doing rounds with real reference frames, commit each improvement, and tear down at the end of each turn.\n   - **Hard constraints (keep verbatim):**\n     - \"commit only, never push\"\n     - \"Don't touch camera.js, player.js, hud.js or character.js. The original session is converting the game to first person in them, on branch hedgerow-poc.\"\n     - \"Never commit Blender preview renders.\"\n     - Never stash, reset or switch branches.\n     - Commit only files I changed.\n     - Put what I did first in reports.\n     - Leave notes in `/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md`.\n   - **Memory rules:**\n     - \"end every browser session and local server used for testing once done\"\n     - verify-headlessly: \"don't reopen the built-in browser pane (preview_start / navigate) for visual checks once the user has closed it … Verify with Node checks … and say plainly in the report which visuals were not seen in a browser. If a look truly needs eyes, ask first.\"\n   - **Peer requests (from the parent session):**\n     - \"Tab 'seed' is yours … please don't use tab-1 or port 8765.\"\n     - Keep ground detail complementary to the parent's `L.clutter` (leaf_litter, rocks_small, branches, rubble_small and others along gutters, the shelled houses, lane and track edges, and behind the MG nests). Fine centimetre-scale pebbles and twigs are OK; never re-place those models there.\n     - \"Please merge hedgerow-poc back before your next round\" (done: 58ae01fe).\n   - **launch.json:** only ever add or remove my own entry, never create or delete the file wholesale. It is not used now, since the server runs from the shell.\n   - **Commit message format:** \"Hedgerow graphics: …\", ending with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n   - **Safety:**\n     - Never accept cookie or consent banners; \"Reject all\" in their settings is OK.\n     - No personal data or age gates.\n     - Reference images are for analysis only. Delete reference screenshots from scratch after comparing.\n     - Downloading files needs permission, so view images through the headless `view` command instead.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Test rig.** No browser pane.\n     - Server: `python3 -I $S/nocache_server.py 8766 <worktree>` (Bash `run_in_background`, `dangerouslyDisableSandbox`); stopped with `pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"`. Exit code 144 on kill is expected.\n     - Headless Chrome via `$S/hl.mjs` (CDP port 9337). Commands: `start <url>` (game URL `http://localhost:8766/fun/hedgerow/?debug&god&go&at=1.5,6`), `eval <file.js>`, `view <url> <out.png>` (new: a throwaway tab plus a screenshot), `stop`; then `rm -rf hl-profile`.\n     - Scripts in `$S = REDACTED`:\n       - `boot.js`, `helpers.js` (snap, snapCrop, stand, startGame), `reload.js`;\n       - `shot.js` (window.__shots `[cx,cz,tx,ty,tz,name,eye=1.65,rel=false]`);\n       - `q_set_{low,med,high}.js` + `q_chk2.js` (compile check per preset);\n       - `fl1.js` (counts bad programs);\n       - `perf0.js` (gpuMs, ab);\n       - `fire_views.js`, `damp_views.js`, `glass_*.js`, `splash_views.js`, `wire_views*.js`, `flare_wire.js`, `flare_prints.js`, `bp_views.js`, `qa_views.js`.\n   - **Checks per commit:**\n     - q_chk2 on low, med and high with no bad programs;\n     - node tests: `for t in fun/hedgerow/tests/*-check.mjs` (9 files: ai, character, clutter, distance, fp, lod, ragdoll, route, world);\n     - `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD hedgerow-poc` must be clean.\n   - **A/B technique:**\n     - Swap a file back to the `git show HEAD:` version, capture, restore. Or toggle uniforms or statics in-page.\n     - Freeze the lights' flicker (`G.lights.statics[].flicker = 0`) when comparing lighting.\n     - Debug-colour masks verify placement (emissive or red overrides).\n   - **Lights (`lights.js`):**\n     - statics carry `fog` and `cone`; flashes carry fog.\n     - Shadow lights shadowOf and shadowOf2 pass fog and cone.\n     - Constants: `CAPPED = 0.1`, `FIRE_FOG = 0.35`.\n   - **Volumetric (`volumetric.js`):**\n     - An analytic airlight per point light, with `uCone[MAX]`.\n     - For capped lamps the stretch is integrated in 6 pieces, weighted by `smoothstep(c, c+0.35, down)*2.2`.\n   - **Fire bounce (`fill.js`):**\n     - `FIRE_UNIFORMS {uFires[4], uBounce}` (materials.js `SMOULDER_UNIFORMS` aliases it).\n     - `addFireBounce(shader, pos, nrm)` adds `fireBounce()` to `irradiance` before `lights_fragment_end`. Terms: size² × wrap / (r² + 4) × 6, gone by 20 m, wrap = clamp(0.35 + 0.65·dot, 0.05, 1).\n   - **Materials (`materials.js` addWeather):**\n     - mDamp and mMud at wall bases, from `shared.grassMap` .w (ground height).\n     - mirrorAlpha feeds SSR only for level water. ssr.js rejects non-level normals; the glass attempt was reverted.\n   - **Decals (`atmosphere.js`):**\n     - 2×2 variant atlases; pinned room per kind.\n     - Kinds: stone, wood, metal, splat, scorch, glass, spall, sign, boot.\n     - `put`/`pin` gained an optional `angle`.\n     - A floor decal's up is world +x; a turn by a carries it to (cos a, −sin a).\n     - Painter: the decal's up is the canvas's down (rows run up v).\n   - **Weather (`weather.js`):**\n     - Rain streak alpha = edge·tail·vAlpha·uOpacity·(uUnlit + uFlash + boost·1.5); `uUnlit` = 0.45.\n     - `setSkyLight` k = min(I,8)·0.04.\n     - Splashes and crowns use `landY` with a world raycast.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (under `fun/hedgerow/js` unless noted):\n   - **cloth.js** (new, 556743c5):\n     - `createSheets(panes, world, terrain, shared, {count=4, seed=41})`.\n     - `facesOf(pr)` caches world triangles; `hanging(p,w)` uses flattened faces, depth(s,u) = outermost d.\n     - Geometry: SX=14, SY=16, pleats, aDu/aDv slopes.\n     - `SHEET_GLSL` `sheetMove()` with gust and lee; normals from finite differences.\n     - customDistance and customDepth materials.\n   - **rooms.js**: `paneRects` returns `prop: pr`.\n   - **signs.js** (new, d3b2687c): `createWaysigns(signposts, matlib)`.\n     - POSTS keyed by `at:[x,z]`; boards [text, paint, N/S/E/W, arrow].\n     - Board shapes from ExtrudeGeometry; canvas 1024×1008 (cells 512×96); the back face is mirrored.\n     - Material via `matlib.resolve`; needs a vertex color attribute.\n   - **levelBuild.js:**\n     - `signposts`, `wrecks` (debris), `wires` (barbed_wire `{x,y,z,yaw,len}`) are collected and returned.\n     - Imports `CAPPED, FIRE_FOG` from lights.js and `rng` from util.\n     - Debris fires are placed via `insideSolid` after the props.\n   - **levels/saint-clair.js**:\n     - `P('signpost', -11.2, 151.8, 90)`;\n     - truck_burnt `{ fire: true, debris: 4 }`;\n     - halftrack_wreck `{ fire: true, debris: 3 }`.\n   - **tools/textures.py** + **assets/textures/cobble*.webp** (7dbc8488): flat-top setts with tilt.\n   - **atmosphere.js**:\n     - ADS[3] = ORTSKOMMANDANTUR; `age` scales the weathering loops.\n     - `bootPrint` painter; boot kind (pinned only, renderOrder 1); `put`/`pin` angle.\n   - **lights.js / volumetric.js / mission.js**: fog and cone plumbing; flak fire FIRE_FOG.\n   - **flames.js**:\n     - PER=5, MAXF=10; h=(1.8+1.1·share)·s, w=(0.95+0.45·share)·s; base f.y−0.25.\n     - Iterates `[effects.fires, effects.debris]`.\n   - **effects.js**:\n     - embers 0.55·k; smoke 0.7·k (#1c1a18 a0.75, size1 (5–8)·s); spark showers f.pop with n scaled by size.\n     - `debris` list, `addDebris`, `burning = [fires, debris]`.\n   - **materials.js**: rising damp (DAMP_GLSL dampNoise, mDamp, mMud, rim); addFireBounce call; SMOULDER_UNIFORMS = FIRE_UNIFORMS.\n   - **fill.js**: FIRE_UNIFORMS, FIRE_BOUNCE_GLSL, addFireBounce.\n   - **terrain.js**: `addFireBounce(shader,'vWPos','normalize(vWNormal)')`.\n   - **weather.js**:\n     - imports SHOT from world.js; `createWeather({..., world})`;\n     - `landY` raycasts from y+30 downward and ignores t<0.01;\n     - main.js passes `world: G.world`.\n   - **wire.js** (new, fd184b5e): `createConcertina(wires)`.\n     - RW=0.0028, SIDES=5, PITCH=0.2, PER=20; tilt=0.42·cos(a/2).\n     - Winding `idx.push(a, b, d, b, e, d)`.\n     - Material `#8a8378` metalness 0.45, roughness 0.36.\n     - The vertex shader widens to `max(RW, dist*0.0011)`.\n   - **prints.js** (new, 2a1466a3): `printBoots(G, lines)`.\n     - Files on LANE and TRACK; stride 0.72; only on mud.\n     - Variants: 0 left / 1 right / 2 scuffed / 3 water-filled; SIZE 0.34.\n   - **main.js**:\n     - imports and calls createSheets, createWaysigns, createConcertina, printBoots;\n     - pinned decals `{stone:480, wood:80, spall:64, sign:5, boot:1100}`;\n     - weather gets `world`.\n   - **README.md**: updated for every commit.\n   - **Shared notes file**: entries for every turn, including the reverted glass attempt and the test-procedure change.\n   - **Read most recently** (`weather.js` rain shader):\n     ```glsl\n     float a = edge * tail * vAlpha * uOpacity * (uUnlit + uFlash + boost * 1.5);\n     gl_FragColor = vec4(uColor * (1.0 + uFlash * 3.0) + lit * 2.0, min(a, 0.9));\n     ```\n     - `rainUniforms`: uColor '#9aa4ad', uUnlit 0.45.\n     - Vertex lighting: `lit += uLightCol[i] / (1.0 + dot(d,d)*0.9)` over 6 lights.\n     - `setSkyLight(color, intensity)`: k = min(intensity,8)·0.04.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **cloth.js:**\n     - GLSL reserved word `out` broke the shader; renamed to `lift`.\n     - Sheets sat inside walls because collision boxes are about 25 cm behind facades; switched to model-face raycasts.\n     - THREE.Raycaster cost 479 ms; switched to flattened-face tests (8 ms).\n   - **Profiling leftovers:** a backup copy saved to a different $TMPDIR left instrumentation in place; removed it manually.\n   - **Fire haze:** caused by the volumetric pass, with the fire light's fog factor ignored. Fixed with FIRE_FOG plumbing.\n   - **Lamp cone:** too weak at first; added ×2.2 gain and a sharper edge.\n   - **Fire A/B:** noisy because of flicker; froze the flicker during the comparison.\n   - **Damp:** invisible at first strength; debug colouring confirmed placement; strength increased.\n   - **Bounce:** lit the ruin's facade through its wall; wrap clamped.\n   - **Window-glass SSR:** no visible gain, because SSR is screen-space and windows mostly reflect dark facades. Reverted.\n   - **Concertina:**\n     - inverted winding;\n     - rust too dark to show at night;\n     - helix looked like a spring, fixed with alternating tilt.\n   - **Signs uv helper:** read transformed positions; fixed to use the untransformed source.\n   - **Browser pane:** the user closed it (memory rule). Switched to a Bash-run server plus the headless `view` command.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Verification:** every improvement was checked with A/B captures and zoomed crops, the per-preset compile check, the node tests, and merge-tree. All commits merge cleanly with hedgerow-poc.\n   - **Performance:**\n     - lamp cones: within noise;\n     - truck fire: about 2.0 ms at close range;\n     - landing raycasts: 0.9 ms per second of splashes;\n     - concertina: 44k triangles, one draw;\n     - boot prints: one instanced draw.\n   - **QA sweep this turn:** twelve route views captured (`$S/snaps/qa01…qa12`, grids `qa_grid0-2`). No obvious faults found.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - All user-role messages were Stop hook feedback repeating \"[constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards aaa game (call of duty, medal of honor). commit each improvement.]\" with growing critiques:\n     - discrete rounds ending in teardown;\n     - few reference frames and self-judged gaps;\n     - nobody saw the changes in a real window;\n     - nothing pushed;\n     - the reverted glass attempt;\n     - latest: \"The commit clause is met: many 'Hedgerow graphics' commits exist, most recently 2a1466a3. The open-ended clause … has no completion criterion in the transcript. The assistant states the work is ongoing, cites no match to AAA parity, and its last message reports headless-only checks and nothing pushed. Iteration is ongoing, so the condition is not yet satisfied.\"\n   - Cross-session messages from the parent session (teammate, not the user):\n     - tab/port note: tab \"seed\" is mine; don't use tab-1 or port 8765;\n     - clutter overlap note: keep mine complementary, don't re-place leaf_litter/rocks_small/branches;\n     - merge requests: hedgerow-poc merged my branch (94022128 → a5c4deff; c5cb31f5 → a0a81b8c, pushed to main); \"Please merge hedgerow-poc back before your next round.\"\n   - A system reminder added the memory \"Verify headlessly\".\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Continue the open-ended improvement loop each turn: real references where possible, commit each improvement, never push.\n   - Report what was not seen in a real browser window.\n   - Tear down at the end of each turn:\n     - `node $S/hl.mjs stop`, then `rm -rf hl-profile`;\n     - `pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"`;\n     - verify no headless processes, port 8766 free, clean tree.\n   - Update the shared notes, then wrap_up and a closing message with what was done first.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Round in progress: a visual QA sweep along the player's route.\n     - Plan: capture views, inspect for faults, fix the clearest, commit; then notes and teardown.\n   - Twelve views were captured; no rendering faults were found.\n   - Observation: \"One thing does stand out in every frame: the rain. Long, evenly bright streaks cover the dark sky even far from any light. At night, rain should be nearly invisible except where a lamp or fire catches it.\"\n   - I was reading the rain shader in `weather.js`:\n     - RAIN_FRAG alpha uses `uUnlit` (0.45) plus boost from vLit and uSky;\n     - RAIN_VERT lights drops by 6 lights;\n     - `setSkyLight` k = min(I,8)·0.04.\n   - No changes made yet this round. The rig is still running: server background task b50gm66s9 on 8766, and the headless Chrome started via hl.mjs.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Continue the investigation just begun: the rain streaks look uniformly bright in dark areas.\n     - Measure the effect of lowering `uUnlit` (0.45), or tying visibility more strongly to local light (vLit/uSky) in `weather.js` RAIN_FRAG.\n     - A/B with headless captures of the lane start and street views (e.g. qa01, qa04).\n     - Commit only if the dark-sky rain becomes subtler while lamp-lit rain still glitters.\n   - Then update the notes and do the full teardown (stop hl.mjs, rm hl-profile, pkill the server, verify), then wrap_up.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/vojta/.REDACTED.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"4d9862ff-008f-41e5-b0e4-38ab270689fa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:22:05.774Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":12,"turnIndex":46},"turnOrigin":"peer","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"4d9862ff-008f-41e5-b0e4-38ab270689fa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/prints.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/prints.js","content":"/* Hedgerow — boot prints in the mud.\n\n   The men who went this way before left their boots in the mud of the\n   sunken lane and the forest track: files of prints along each, a pace\n   apart, left and right a hand's breadth either side of the line each man\n   walked, some going up towards the village and some coming back, every so\n   often one missing (trodden over, washed out), one scuffed where a heel\n   slid, one with the rain standing in it; only where the ground is mud,\n   not on the cobbles, the grass or the leaf litter. Pinned decals\n   (atmosphere.js 'boot'), turned along the way each man went, laid on the\n   slope of the ground. */\n\nimport { rng } from './util.js';\n\nconst STRIDE = 0.72;        // m from one foot's print to the other's\nconst SIZE = 0.34;          // the decal, across (a boot ~29 cm long in it)\n\n/* G: its terrain and decals; lines: the level's (LANE, TRACK). How many were put down. */\nexport function printBoots(G, lines, { seed = 1944 } = {}) {\n  const R = rng(seed), decals = G.decals, terrain = G.terrain;\n  // the files: [line, how far across it each man walked (m), which way: 1 up it, -1 back]\n  const files = [[lines.LANE, -0.9, 1], [lines.LANE, 0.75, 1], [lines.LANE, 0.1, -1],\n    [lines.TRACK, -0.7, 1], [lines.TRACK, 0.85, -1]];\n  let n = 0;\n  for (const [line, off, way] of files) {\n    if (!line) continue;\n    let s = R() * STRIDE, foot = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < line.length - 1; i++) {\n      const [x0, z0] = line[i], [x1, z1] = line[i + 1];\n      const len = Math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0);\n      if (len < 1e-6) continue;\n      const dx = (x1 - x0) / len, dz = (z1 - z0) / len;\n      for (; s < len; s += STRIDE * (0.92 + R() * 0.16)) {\n        foot ^= 1;\n        if (R() < 0.22) continue;\n        // the right foot to the right of the way he went ((-dz, dx) is right of (dx, dz))\n        const across = (foot ? 1 : -1) * way * 0.11 + off + (R() - 0.5) * 0.14;\n        const x = x0 + dx * s - dz * across, z = z0 + dz * s + dx * across;\n        if (terrain.surfaceAt(x, z) !== 'mud') continue;\n        const nn = terrain.normal(x, z);\n        // the decal's up (its toe) turned onto the way he went: a turn a carries +x to (cos a, -sin a)\n        const angle = Math.atan2(-dz * way, dx * way) + (R() - 0.5) * 0.25;\n        const r = R(), variant = r < 0.1 ? 2 : r < 0.22 ? 3 : foot;\n        if (!decals.pin('boot', x, terrain.height(x, z), z, nn[0], nn[1], nn[2], SIZE, false, R, true, variant, angle)) return n;\n        n++;\n      }\n      s -= len;\n    }\n  }\n  return n;\n}\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/prints.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3e3631d2-cea9-48a4-bc3e-4976b6d41240","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:22:06.110Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/prints.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t/* Hedgerow — boot prints in the mud.\n2\t\n3\t   The men who went this way before left their boots in the mud of the\n4\t   sunken lane and the forest track: files of prints along each, a pace\n5\t   apart, left and right a hand's breadth either side of the line each man\n6\t   walked, some going up towards the village and some coming back, every so\n7\t   often one missing (trodden over, washed out), one scuffed where a heel\n8\t   slid, one with the rain standing in it; only where the ground is mud,\n9\t   not on the cobbles, the grass or the leaf litter. Pinned decals\n10\t   (atmosphere.js 'boot'), turned along the way each man went, laid on the\n11\t   slope of the ground. */\n12\t\n13\timport { rng } from './util.js';\n14\t\n15\tconst STRIDE = 0.72;        // m from one foot's print to the other's\n16\tconst SIZE = 0.34;          // the decal, across (a boot ~29 cm long in it)\n17\t\n18\t/* G: its terrain and decals; lines: the level's (LANE, TRACK). How many were put down. */\n19\texport function printBoots(G, lines, { seed = 1944 } = {}) {\n20\t  const R = rng(seed), decals = G.decals, terrain = G.terrain;\n21\t  // the files: [line, how far across it each man walked (m), which way: 1 up it, -1 back]\n22\t  const files = [[lines.LANE, -0.9, 1], [lines.LANE, 0.75, 1], [lines.LANE, 0.1, -1],\n23\t    [lines.TRACK, -0.7, 1], [lines.TRACK, 0.85, -1]];\n24\t  let n = 0;\n25\t  for (const [line, off, way] of files) {\n26\t    if (!line) continue;\n27\t    let s = R() * STRIDE, foot = 0;\n28\t    for (let i = 0; i < line.length - 1; i++) {\n29\t      const [x0, z0] = line[i], [x1, z1] = line[i + 1];\n30\t      const len = Math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0);\n31\t      if (len < 1e-6) continue;\n32\t      const dx = (x1 - x0) / len, dz = (z1 - z0) / len;\n33\t      for (; s < len; s += STRIDE * (0.92 + R() * 0.16)) {\n34\t        foot ^= 1;\n35\t        if (R() < 0.22) continue;\n36\t        // the right foot to the right of the way he went ((-dz, dx) is right of (dx, dz))\n37\t        const across = (foot ? 1 : -1) * way * 0.11 + off + (R() - 0.5) * 0.14;\n38\t        const x = x0 + dx * s - dz * across, z = z0 + dz * s + dx * across;\n39\t        if (terrain.surfaceAt(x, z) !== 'mud') continue;\n40\t        const nn = terrain.normal(x, z);\n41\t        // the decal's up (its toe) turned onto the way he went: a turn a carries +x to (cos a, -sin a)\n42\t        const angle = Math.atan2(-dz * way, dx * way) + (R() - 0.5) * 0.25;\n43\t        const r = R(), variant = r < 0.1 ? 2 : r < 0.22 ? 3 : foot;\n44\t        if (!decals.pin('boot', x, terrain.height(x, z), z, nn[0], nn[1], nn[2], SIZE, false, R, true, variant, angle)) return n;\n45\t        n++;\n46\t      }\n47\t      s -= len;\n48\t    }\n49\t  }\n50\t  return n;\n51\t}\n52\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"3e3631d2-cea9-48a4-bc3e-4976b6d41240","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js","content":"/* Hedgerow — concertina wire.\n\n   Along each of the level's barbed-wire obstacles (the knife rests strung\n   with a few strands) a coil of concertina lies on the ground, the wire\n   every assault on a Normandy position ran into: loops of rusted steel\n   some 85 cm across, each a little different, the coil sagging and leaning\n   as it was dragged out and dropped, wet and catching the light of the\n   lamps, the fires and a flare in glints along its loops. One mesh, each\n   loop a thin tube that is never thinner on screen than about a pixel (its\n   vertex shader widens it with distance): from afar the coil reads as a\n   dark tangle over the ground, close by as wire. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { rng } from './util.js';\nimport { dimFillSpecular } from './fill.js';\n\nconst RW = 0.0028;        // the wire's radius (m)\nconst SIDES = 5;          // round the wire\nconst PITCH = 0.2;        // m along the coil from one loop to the next\nconst PER = 20;           // samples along a loop\n\n/* wires: the obstacles as levelBuild placed them ({x, y, z, yaw, len} in metres and radians) */\nexport function createConcertina(wires, { seed = 7 } = {}) {\n  if (!wires.length) return null;\n  const R = rng(seed);\n  const pos = [], ctr = [], nrm = [], idx = [];\n  const C = new THREE.Vector3(), Cn = new THREE.Vector3(), T = new THREE.Vector3(), N = new THREE.Vector3(), B = new THREE.Vector3();\n  const X = new THREE.Vector3();\n  for (const w of wires) {\n    const r0 = 0.4 + R() * 0.05, turns = Math.max(6, Math.round(w.len / PITCH)), steps = turns * PER;\n    const c = Math.cos(w.yaw), s = Math.sin(w.yaw);\n    X.set(c, 0, -s);\n    const lean = (R() - 0.5) * 0.3, sag = 0.05 + R() * 0.05, ph = R() * 6.28;\n    // the coil's centre line at t (0..1 along it): loops of their own size, sagging between its\n    // ends, leaning a little to one side\n    const at = (t, out) => {\n      const a = t * turns * Math.PI * 2;\n      const k = 0.9 + 0.1 * (1 + Math.sin(a * 0.43 + ph) * 0.6 + Math.sin(a * 0.17 + ph * 2.3) * 0.4);\n      const r = r0 * k * (1 - sag * Math.sin(Math.PI * t) * 1.5);\n      // its loops clipped to each other alternately, so as it was pulled out they lean one way and\n      // the next the other and cross: the diamonds of concertina, not a spring\n      const tilt = 0.42 * Math.cos(a * 0.5);\n      const lx = (t - 0.5) * w.len + r * Math.sin(a) * Math.sin(tilt);\n      const ly = r * 0.92 + r * Math.cos(a) * 0.86 + lean * r * Math.sin(a) * 0.25;\n      const lz = r * Math.sin(a) * Math.cos(tilt) + lean * 0.08;\n      return out.set(w.x + lx * c + lz * s, w.y + ly, w.z - lx * s + lz * c);\n    };\n    const base = ctr.length / 3;\n    for (let i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\n      const t = i / steps;\n      at(t, C);\n      at(Math.min(1, t + 1e-4), Cn);\n      T.subVectors(Cn, C).normalize();\n      if (i === steps) { at(t - 1e-4, Cn); T.subVectors(C, Cn).normalize(); }\n      N.crossVectors(T, X).normalize();\n      B.crossVectors(T, N).normalize();\n      for (let j = 0; j < SIDES; j++) {\n        const q = (j / SIDES) * Math.PI * 2, nx = N.x * Math.cos(q) + B.x * Math.sin(q), ny = N.y * Math.cos(q) + B.y * Math.sin(q), nz = N.z * Math.cos(q) + B.z * Math.sin(q);\n        ctr.push(C.x, C.y, C.z);\n        nrm.push(nx, ny, nz);\n        pos.push(C.x + nx * RW, C.y + ny * RW, C.z + nz * RW);\n      }\n    }\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\n      for (let j = 0; j < SIDES; j++) {\n        const a = base + i * SIDES + j, b = base + i * SIDES + (j + 1) % SIDES, d = a + SIDES, e = b + SIDES;\n        idx.push(a, b, d, b, e, d);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n  geo.setAttribute('normal', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(nrm, 3));\n  geo.setAttribute('aCenter', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(ctr, 3));\n  geo.setIndex(idx);\n  geo.computeBoundingSphere();\n  geo.boundingSphere.radius += 1;\n  // weathered galvanised steel, rust coming through, wet: a grey that takes the light of the sky,\n  // glossy with the rain, catching the lamps and a flare in glints\n  const mat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: '#8a8378', roughness: 0.36, metalness: 0.45 });\n  mat.name = 'concertina';\n  mat.onBeforeCompile = (shader) => {\n    shader.vertexShader = shader.vertexShader\n      .replace('#include <common>', '#include <common>\\nattribute vec3 aCenter;')\n      // never thinner than about a pixel: a coil 30 m off stays a tangle, not a flicker\n      .replace('#include <begin_vertex>', `vec3 transformed = aCenter + objectNormal * max(${RW}, length(aCenter - cameraPosition) * 0.0011);`);\n    dimFillSpecular(shader);\n  };\n  mat.customProgramCacheKey = () => 'hedgerow-concertina';\n  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  mesh.name = 'concertina';\n  mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n  return mesh;\n}\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b8406cd4-87cb-4400-b3ab-eacf7cc41e39","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:22:06.110Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/wire.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t/* Hedgerow — concertina wire.\n2\t\n3\t   Along each of the level's barbed-wire obstacles (the knife rests strung\n4\t   with a few strands) a coil of concertina lies on the ground, the wire\n5\t   every assault on a Normandy position ran into: loops of rusted steel\n6\t   some 85 cm across, each a little different, the coil sagging and leaning\n7\t   as it was dragged out and dropped, wet and catching the light of the\n8\t   lamps, the fires and a flare in glints along its loops. One mesh, each\n9\t   loop a thin tube that is never thinner on screen than about a pixel (its\n10\t   vertex shader widens it with distance): from afar the coil reads as a\n11\t   dark tangle over the ground, close by as wire. */\n12\t\n13\timport * as THREE from 'three';\n14\timport { rng } from './util.js';\n15\timport { dimFillSpecular } from './fill.js';\n16\t\n17\tconst RW = 0.0028;        // the wire's radius (m)\n18\tconst SIDES = 5;          // round the wire\n19\tconst PITCH = 0.2;        // m along the coil from one loop to the next\n20\tconst PER = 20;           // samples along a loop\n21\t\n22\t/* wires: the obstacles as levelBuild placed them ({x, y, z, yaw, len} in metres and radians) */\n23\texport function createConcertina(wires, { seed = 7 } = {}) {\n24\t  if (!wires.length) return null;\n25\t  const R = rng(seed);\n26\t  const pos = [], ctr = [], nrm = [], idx = [];\n27\t  const C = new THREE.Vector3(), Cn = new THREE.Vector3(), T = new THREE.Vector3(), N = new THREE.Vector3(), B = new THREE.Vector3();\n28\t  const X = new THREE.Vector3();\n29\t  for (const w of wires) {\n30\t    const r0 = 0.4 + R() * 0.05, turns = Math.max(6, Math.round(w.len / PITCH)), steps = turns * PER;\n31\t    const c = Math.cos(w.yaw), s = Math.sin(w.yaw);\n32\t    X.set(c, 0, -s);\n33\t    const lean = (R() - 0.5) * 0.3, sag = 0.05 + R() * 0.05, ph = R() * 6.28;\n34\t    // the coil's centre line at t (0..1 along it): loops of their own size, sagging between its\n35\t    // ends, leaning a little to one side\n36\t    const at = (t, out) => {\n37\t      const a = t * turns * Math.PI * 2;\n38\t      const k = 0.9 + 0.1 * (1 + Math.sin(a * 0.43 + ph) * 0.6 + Math.sin(a * 0.17 + ph * 2.3) * 0.4);\n39\t      const r = r0 * k * (1 - sag * Math.sin(Math.PI * t) * 1.5);\n40\t      // its loops clipped to each other alternately, so as it was pulled out they lean one way and\n41\t      // the next the other and cross: the diamonds of concertina, not a spring\n42\t      const tilt = 0.42 * Math.cos(a * 0.5);\n43\t      const lx = (t - 0.5) * w.len + r * Math.sin(a) * Math.sin(tilt);\n44\t      const ly = r * 0.92 + r * Math.cos(a) * 0.86 + lean * r * Math.sin(a) * 0.25;\n45\t      const lz = r * Math.sin(a) * Math.cos(tilt) + lean * 0.08;\n46\t      return out.set(w.x + lx * c + lz * s, w.y + ly, w.z - lx * s + lz * c);\n47\t    };\n48\t    const base = ctr.length / 3;\n49\t    for (let i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\n50\t      const t = i / steps;\n51\t      at(t, C);\n52\t      at(Math.min(1, t + 1e-4), Cn);\n53\t      T.subVectors(Cn, C).normalize();\n54\t      if (i === steps) { at(t - 1e-4, Cn); T.subVectors(C, Cn).normalize(); }\n55\t      N.crossVectors(T, X).normalize();\n56\t      B.crossVectors(T, N).normalize();\n57\t      for (let j = 0; j < SIDES; j++) {\n58\t        const q = (j / SIDES) * Math.PI * 2, nx = N.x * Math.cos(q) + B.x * Math.sin(q), ny = N.y * Math.cos(q) + B.y * Math.sin(q), nz = N.z * Math.cos(q) + B.z * Math.sin(q);\n59\t        ctr.push(C.x, C.y, C.z);\n60\t        nrm.push(nx, ny, nz);\n61\t        pos.push(C.x + nx * RW, C.y + ny * RW, C.z + nz * RW);\n62\t      }\n63\t    }\n64\t    for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\n65\t      for (let j = 0; j < SIDES; j++) {\n66\t        const a = base + i * SIDES + j, b = base + i * SIDES + (j + 1) % SIDES, d = a + SIDES, e = b + SIDES;\n67\t        idx.push(a, b, d, b, e, d);\n68\t      }\n69\t    }\n70\t  }\n71\t  const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n72\t  geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n73\t  geo.setAttribute('normal', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(nrm, 3));\n74\t  geo.setAttribute('aCenter', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(ctr, 3));\n75\t  geo.setIndex(idx);\n76\t  geo.computeBoundingSphere();\n77\t  geo.boundingSphere.radius += 1;\n78\t  // weathered galvanised steel, rust coming through, wet: a grey that takes the light of the sky,\n79\t  // glossy with the rain, catching the lamps and a flare in glints\n80\t  const mat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: '#8a8378', roughness: 0.36, metalness: 0.45 });\n81\t  mat.name = 'concertina';\n82\t  mat.onBeforeCompile = (shader) => {\n83\t    shader.vertexShader = shader.vertexShader\n84\t      .replace('#include <common>', '#include <common>\\nattribute vec3 aCenter;')\n85\t      // never thinner than about a pixel: a coil 30 m off stays a tangle, not a flicker\n86\t      .replace('#include <begin_vertex>', `vec3 transformed = aCenter + objectNormal * max(${RW}, length(aCenter - cameraPosition) * 0.0011);`);\n87\t    dimFillSpecular(shader);\n88\t  };\n89\t  mat.customProgramCacheKey = () => 'hedgerow-concertina';\n90\t  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n91\t  mesh.name = 'concertina';\n92\t  mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n93\t  return mesh;\n94\t}\n95\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
